   "source": [
    "### Supported Data Types"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c6e9ae67",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The `resplotclass` supports a variety of data types, including `xarray.DataArray`, `xarray.Dataset`, `xugri.UgridDataArray`, `xugrid.UgridDataset`, and `geopandas.GeoDataFrame`. These types contain both the data, metadata and coordinate reference system (CRS). Here, a CRS is added to the `xugrid.UgridDataArray` as it is generally not included in the netCDF file.\n",
    "\n",
    "To read the data required for this notebook, use the following code:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "992d8556",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Packages\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "\n",
    "import geopandas as gpd\n",
    "import rioxarray as rxr\n",
    "import xugrid as xu\n",
    "\n",
    "# Directories\n",
    "dir_path_repo = next(p for p in Path.cwd().resolve().parents if p.name == \"resplotlib\")\n",
    "dir_path_data = dir_path_repo / \"data\"\n",
    "\n",
    "# Read data\n",
    "da_bathymetry = rxr.open_rasterio(dir_path_data / \"bathymetry.tif\").squeeze()\n",
    "da_image = rxr.open_rasterio(dir_path_data / \"image.tif\").squeeze()\n",
    "uds_model = xu.open_dataset(dir_path_data / \"model.nc\")\n",
    "gdf_points = gpd.read_file(dir_path_data / \"points.geojson\")\n",
    "gdf_lines = gpd.read_file(dir_path_data / \"shorelines.geojson\")\n",
    "gdf_polygons = gpd.read_file(dir_path_data / \"polygons.geojson\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Add a coordinate reference system (CRS)\n",
    "uds_model.ugrid.set_crs(\"EPSG:32631\", allow_override=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Get bounds and limits\n",
    "bounds = da_bathymetry.rio.bounds()\n",
    "xlim = (bounds[0], bounds[2])\n",
    "ylim = (bounds[1], bounds[3])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d86b893d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Static plotting"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "f45903c7",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The `resplotclass` provides the following static plot methods: `imshow`, `pcolormesh`, `contourf`, `quiver`, `streamplot`, `geometries`, `basemap`. Moreover, the following methods are available to create a figure and axes, show the plot and save the plot: `figure`, `axes`, `show` and `save`. To find out more about static plotting, see the [Static plotting notebook](./03_static_plotting.ipynb).\n",
    "\n",
    "Here a figure and axes are created using the `figure` and `axes` methods of the `resplotclass`. The `imshow` method is used to plot an `xarray.DataArray` and `xugrid.UgridDataArray`, while the `geometries` method is used to plot a `geopandas.GeoDataFrame`. Basemaps are added to the axes using the `basemap` method. Finally, the plot is shown using the `show` method."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "8dadf1fd",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Initialise figure and axes\n",
    "fig, axs = rpc.subplots(2, 2, figsize=(16, 10))\n",
    "axs = axs.flatten()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Plot bathymetry\n",
    "rpc.imshow(da=da_bathymetry, ax=axs[0], style=\"bathymetry\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Plot image\n",
    "rpc.imshow(da=da_image, ax=axs[1], style=\"image\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Plot elevation\n",
    "rpc.imshow(uda=uds_model[\"mesh2d_mor_bl\"], ax=axs[2], robust=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Plot geometries\n",
    "rpc.geometries(gdf=gdf_points, ax=axs[3], color=\"blue\", label=\"Points\")\n",
    "rpc.geometries(gdf=gdf_lines, ax=axs[3], column=\"year\", cmap=\"Spectral_r\", legend=True, legend_kwds={\"label\": \"Year [-]\"})\n",
    "rpc.geometries(gdf=gdf_polygons, ax=axs[3], facecolor=\"none\", edgecolor=\"red\", label=\"Polygons\")\n",
    "axs[3].legend(loc=\"upper right\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Plot basemaps\n",
    "for ax in axs:\n",
    "    rpc.basemap(crs=\"EPSG:32631\", ax=ax, style=\"light\", xlim=xlim, ylim=ylim)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Show image\n",
    "rpc.show(fig)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "80890670",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Interactive plotting"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "da2ae3d3",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The `resplotclass` provides the following interactive plot methods: `explore_data`, `explore_geometries`, `explore_basemap`. Morever, the following methods are available to create a map, show the map and save the map: `Map`, `show` and `save`. The `Map` method creates an interactive map using `ipyleaflet`, which allows users to interact with the map and the plotted data. The `Map` method also contains a draw control layer, which allows users to interactively draw and edit geometries on the map. The map contain various methods to retrieve information about the map, such as the current view bounds, zoom level and drawn geometries. To find out more about interactive plotting, see the [Interactive plotting notebook](./04_interactive_plotting.ipynb).\n",
    "\n",
    "Here, the `Map` method is used to create a map. A `geopandas.GeoDataFrame` is supplied to the `Map` and set to the map's draw control layer. This is a layer in which the user can interactively draw and edit geometries. The `explore_data` method is used to plot an `xarray.DataArray` and `xugrid.UgridDataArray`, while the `explore_geometries` method is used to plot a `geopandas.GeoDataFrame`. Basemaps are added to the axes using the `explore_basemap` method. Finally, the map is shown using the `show` method.\n",
    "\n",
    "Next, current view bounds, zoom level and drawn geometries are retrieved from the map using the `get_view_bounds()`, `get_view_zoom_levels()` and `get_drawn_geometries()` methods of the `Map`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "ebe53914",
   "metadata": {},
